# Owner approval keys (claude-agents decision 0114 section 2), OpenSSH allowed_signers format:
#   owner@stigready namespaces="stigready-owner-approval" sk-ssh-ed25519@openssh.com AAAA... <comment>
# Only FIDO2 security keys (sk-ssh-ed25519@openssh.com, sk-ecdsa-sha2-nistp256@openssh.com) count: a signature needs a
# physical touch, so the program agent, which shares the owner's GitHub login, cannot make one. The removal gate reads
# this file from the BASE branch, never from the pull request. Changing it is itself a removal-class change that
# needs a signature by a key already listed. While no key is listed, the PR that adds the first key must be signed by
# that key.
#
# The owner adds the key (a physical step): ssh-keygen -t ed25519-sk -O resident -O verify-required -C owner-approval
# then a PR adding:  owner@stigready namespaces="stigready-owner-approval" <contents of the .pub file>
